ERASE-CARE-DATA

Requested 2026-10-03 by the owner, in writing, three times: the care rows now in
production describe the pre-rebuild product that was rejected, and reading them
beside package-first data misleads. They asked for them to be erased so testing
can start from nothing, and for the account to survive so signing in still works.

What goes: people, the medication catalog, packages, the whole inventory ledger,
plans and their versions, recorded doses with their allocations and corrections,
count sessions, refill settings, sync receipts.

What stays: accounts, sessions, households, memberships, subscriptions. Nothing
that stays references anything that goes — accounts and households are the parents
of care data, never its children — which is what makes this safe to do in one
transaction.

The only way back is the backup the script dumps and reads back before it starts.

This file is the confirmation. Remove it once the purge has run; the run that sees
it gone reports that there is nothing to do and passes.
